import FreeFermionGraphs.Theorem3EvenHoleFree
import FreeFermionGraphs.KrylovRowClosedFormHoles
import FreeFermionGraphs.HoleAttachment
import FreeFermionGraphs.PauliEvenHoopIdentity
import FreeFermionGraphs.PauliHoleOperator
import FreeFermionGraphs.CliqueHoppingMatrix
import FreeFermionGraphs.TheoremOneII

/-!
# Theorem 3 (Polynomial Divisibility) on a symmetry sector, for a general claw-free graph

Manuscript reference: arXiv 2305.15625v1, Theorem 3 `theorem:polynomialdivisibility`
(L1328-1336), its proof (induction on `k`, L1494-1520; case (b.iv), the hole terms,
L1527-1576), Result 2 (L110-127) and Eq. (decoratedtree) (L1434-1445).  (The repo numbers some
lemmas of v1 differently, following a revised manuscript that is not available.)

This file proves Theorem 3 for a finite claw-free graph `G` *with* even holes, a simplicial clique
`K` and a Pauli clique Hamiltonian representation `H`, on a symmetry sector.  The even-hole-free
case (where there is no sector) is `Theorem3EvenHoleFree.lean`.

## The statement

v1 states the theorem existentially: over each mutual eigenspace `𝒥` of the generalized cycle
symmetries `J_c`, `Π_𝒥 ad_{iH}^k χ = (-2i)^k ∑_P (A_{G,𝒥}^k)_{{j*},P} h_P` for a real matrix
`A_{G,𝒥}` that is the weighted adjacency matrix of a directed bipartite graph.  The matrix is only
*proposed* later, in Eq. (decoratedtree) (L1434-1445).  Here the matrix is the corrected matrix
`A_λ = cliqueHoppingMatrix G K b lam` of `CliqueHoppingMatrix.lean` (sign `(-1)^{k-1}`, root-handle
arcs, per-event normalisation `1/|c|`), and the content is the identity, in the Lean convention
`[H, ·]` (without the factor `i` of `[iH, ·]`),

`[H, ·]^k (χ) · Pr = (-2)^k ∑_P ((A_λ^k)_{{j*},P}) h_P Pr`

for every `Pr` with `[H, Pr] = 0` and `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr` for every class `c` of even holes.

*Reading of "over each mutual eigenspace".*  The left side `Π_𝒥 ad^k χ` of v1 and the right side
without `Π_𝒥` are only consistent after restricting both to the eigenspace; `J_c` need not
commute with the individual path operators `h_P`, so the faithful reading is right multiplication
by `Pr` (`ad^k χ` itself commutes with `J_c`: `[χ, J_c] = 0` by Result 2, and `[H, J_c] = 0` by
Theorem 1(ii)).  `Pr² = Pr` is never used and is not assumed, so the theorem holds for every such
`Pr`, in particular for the joint spectral projector `Π_𝒥`.

## Main declarations

* `SimpleGraph.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation.paperTheorem3_of_commute`: the concrete form,
  with the premises `[H, Pr] = 0` and `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr` (`hJ`, over the classes of even holes
  only) made explicit.
* `paperTheorem3_of_cycleAlgebra`: the same for `Pr` in the subalgebra generated by the cycle
  operators `J_c` (for example the joint spectral projector, a polynomial in the commuting `J_c`);
  `[H, Pr] = 0` is then discharged by Theorem 1(ii).
* `paperTheorem3_of_commute_exists`: the existential form of v1 over `ℝ`, with witness `A_λ`, a
  real matrix that is bipartite by the parity of the path length.
* `RootedInducedPath.IsSectorBalancedRow`, `isSectorBalancedRow_cliqueHoppingMatrix_pow_root`: the
  rows `(A_λ^n)_{{j*},·}` are constant along deformation closures, wand reversals, and the sources
  of one handle and one class of even hoops (v1 Lemma `deformationclosurepathsrelation` and Eq.
  (pathcircle), from the closed form of `KrylovRowClosedFormHoles.lean`).
* `commutator_sum_mul_of_isSectorBalancedRow`: the one-step identity
  `[H, ∑_P c_P h_P Pr] = ∑_Q (-2 ∑_P c_P (A_λ)_{PQ}) h_Q Pr` for sector-balanced rows `c`.
* `holeEvents_fibre_card`, `sum_holeEvents_general`: each hole attached to a handle `Q` is the hoop
  carrier of exactly two wand events with handle `Q`, for an arbitrary summand (the fibre form of
  `card_evenHoopEvents`); needed because the operator `h_C` is not constant on a deformation class.

## Proof

Induction on `k` through `iteratedCommutator_eq_matrixPow_sum_of_rows` in the basis
`P ↦ h_P Pr`.  Since `[H, Pr] = 0`, `[H, X Pr] = [H, X] Pr`, and one step on a sector-balanced row
`c` is, by the exact one-row decomposition of `KrylovRowDecomposition.lean`:

* the tree part gives `∑_Q (∑_P c_P T_{PQ}) h_Q`;
* the clone terms `h_P h_j`, `j ∈ D(P)`, cancel in pairs `P ↔ P~` for a deformation-balanced row
  (`sum_deformation_smul_eq_zero`);
* the terms of the odd wands cancel in pairs `P ↔ P*` (`sum_oddWand_smul_eq_zero`, from the wand
  pairing `h_P h_j = -h_{P*} h_{j_{s+1}}`);
* the terms of the even wands are grouped by the handle `Q`: by the even-hoop identity
  `h_P h_j = (-1)^{k-1} h_Q h_C` (`pathOperator_mul_bubble_eq_holeOperatorOfCarrier`) and the
  two-to-one correspondence of events and attached holes (`sum_holeEvents_general`), the events of
  a handle and class `c` contribute `2 c_c (-1)^{k-1} h_Q ∑_{C ∈ c} h_C = 2 c_c (-1)^{k-1} h_Q J_c`,
  and `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr`.  On the other side the hoop part of `A_λ` gives the column total
  `|c| · (-1)^{k-1} λ_c/|c| · 2` (`sum_attachedHoles_holeOperator_mul`: the attached holes of a class
  are its whole deformation closure, `|⟨C₀⟩| = |c|`).

## Fidelity

* *Names.*  The unqualified name `paperTheorem3` is reserved for the statement of v1, in which `Pr`
  is the projector `Π_𝒥` onto a mutual eigenspace of the `J_c`.  The abstract operator algebra `A`
  has no spectral theory, so `Pr` is an element of `A` with the stated properties and the names
  carry the suffix `_of_commute` (premise `[H, Pr] = 0`) and `_of_cycleAlgebra` (premise: `Pr`
  lies in the algebra generated by the `J_c`), as required by `docs/PAPER_FIDELITY.md`.  No
  structure field or certificate assumes a claim that is to be proved.
* *The matrix.*  The matrix is the corrected one of `CliqueHoppingMatrix.lean`, not the printed
  Eq. (decoratedtree) (which misses the sign `(-1)^{k-1}` of `h_P h_j = (-1)^{k-1} h_{P_s} h_C`
  and the root arcs, and normalises per target instead of per bubble event): with the printed
  weights the identity fails already for the four-cycle with `K` an edge.  The corrected matrix
  is real for real `λ` (`cliqueHoppingMatrix_map`) and bipartite
  (`cliqueHoppingMatrix_ne_zero_imp_odd`).
* *The sector hypothesis.*  `hJ` quantifies only over classes of genuine even holes (carriers of
  full-cyclic labellings): the quotient `EvenHoleDeformationClass` also contains the singleton
  classes of non-hole sets, on which `J_c = 0`, and `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr` would force `λ_c Pr = 0`.
* *Scalars.*  `R` is a field of characteristic zero, so that the class sizes `|c|` are invertible
  (the weights of the hoop part are `λ_c/|c|` per event).
* *What is not proved here.*  v1's `Π_𝒥` as an actual spectral projector, and Theorem 1(iii)
  (`[J_c, J_{c'}] = 0`) which makes the sector decomposition possible, are assembled elsewhere
  (`JointSpectralProjections.lean`, `CycleSymmetrySectors.lean`); here they enter only through the
  hypotheses on `Pr`.
-/

open scoped BigOperators

universe u v w

variable {V : Type u}

namespace SimpleGraph

variable {G : SimpleGraph V} {K : Set V}

/-! ### The events of a handle: every attached hole is hit exactly twice -/

section Events

open Classical

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]

/-- **Each hole attached to `Q` is the hoop carrier of exactly two wand events with handle `Q`**
(and an even hoop): the event `(P, j)` and its reversal `(P*, j_{s+1})`.  This is the fibre
statement inside the proof of `card_evenHoopEvents` (v1 L1555-1576: every hole of `⟨C₀⟩` occurs
at the handle twice, the two directions around the hole); it is needed here for a summand that
is not constant on a deformation class (the operator `h_C`). -/
theorem holeEvents_fibre_card (Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K) {C : Set V}
    (hC : C ∈ attachedHoles G K Q) :
    ((holeEvents G K Q).filter fun e => bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2 = C).card = 2 := by
  set Ev := holeEvents G K Q with hEv
  let φ : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K × V → Set V :=
    fun e => bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2
  have hφ : ∀ (e : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K × V) (w : CliqueBubbleWand G K e.1),
      w.handle = Q → w.bubble = e.2 → φ e = w.hoopCarrier := by
    intro e w hh hb
    unfold φ CliqueBubbleWand.hoopCarrier
    rw [hh, hb]
  obtain ⟨⟨H, hHev, hHC⟩, hQC⟩ := mem_attachedHoles.1 hC
  have hQH : Q.HoleAttached (Set.range H.vertex) := hHC ▸ hQC
  obtain ⟨P, w, hh, hcar⟩ :=
    RootedInducedPath.exists_cliqueBubbleWand_of_holeAttached H hQH
  rw [hHC] at hcar
  have hw_ev : Even w.hoopCard :=
    w.even_hoopCard_of_range_eq H hHev (hcar.trans hHC.symm)
  have hh2 : w.reverseWand.handle = Q := w.reverseWand_handle.trans hh
  have hcar2 : w.reverseWand.hoopCarrier = C := w.reverseWand_hoopCarrier.trans hcar
  have hev2 : Even w.reverseWand.hoopCard := by
    rw [w.reverseWand_hoopCard]
    exact hw_ev
  have he1 : (P, w.bubble) ∈ Ev ∧ φ (P, w.bubble) = C := by
    refine ⟨?_, (hφ (P, w.bubble) w hh rfl).trans hcar⟩
    rw [hEv, holeEvents, Finset.mem_filter]
    exact ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, w, rfl, hh, hw_ev⟩
  have he2 : (w.reverse, w.reverseBubble) ∈ Ev ∧ φ (w.reverse, w.reverseBubble) = C := by
    refine ⟨?_, (hφ (w.reverse, w.reverseBubble) w.reverseWand hh2 rfl).trans hcar2⟩
    rw [hEv, holeEvents, Finset.mem_filter]
    exact ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, w.reverseWand, rfl, hh2, hev2⟩
  have hne : ((P, w.bubble) : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K × V) ≠
      (w.reverse, w.reverseBubble) :=
    fun h => w.adj_bubble_reverseBubble.ne (congrArg Prod.snd h)
  rw [Finset.card_eq_two]
  refine ⟨(P, w.bubble), (w.reverse, w.reverseBubble), hne, ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨-, -, x, y, hx, hy, hxy, hΓ⟩ := hQC
  -- a bubble of a wand with handle `Q` and hoop carrier `C` is `x` or `y`
  have hbub : ∀ {P' : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K} (w' : CliqueBubbleWand G K P'),
      w'.handle = Q → w'.hoopCarrier = C → w'.bubble = x ∨ w'.bubble = y := by
    intro P' w' hh' hc'
    refine (hΓ w'.bubble (hc' ▸ w'.bubble_mem_hoopCarrier)).1 ?_
    have := w'.adj_handle_terminalVertex
    rwa [hh'] at this
  ext e
  simp only [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨he, hφe⟩
    rw [hEv, holeEvents, Finset.mem_filter] at he
    obtain ⟨-, w', hb', hh', -⟩ := he
    have hc' : w'.hoopCarrier = C := by rw [← hφ e w' hh' hb']; exact hφe
    have hj : e.2 = w.bubble ∨ e.2 = w.reverseBubble := by
      have h1 := hbub w' hh' hc'
      have h2 := hbub w hh hcar
      have h3 := hbub w.reverseWand hh2 hcar2
      have h4 := w.adj_bubble_reverseBubble.ne
      rw [hb'] at h1
      change e.2 = x ∨ e.2 = y at h1
      change w.bubble = x ∨ w.bubble = y at h2
      change w.reverseBubble = x ∨ w.reverseBubble = y at h3
      rcases h1 with h1 | h1 <;> rcases h2 with h2 | h2 <;> rcases h3 with h3 | h3 <;>
        first
        | exact Or.inl (h1.trans h2.symm)
        | exact Or.inr (h1.trans h3.symm)
        | exact absurd (h2.trans h3.symm) h4
    rcases hj with hj | hj
    · left
      exact Prod.ext (w.eq_of_handle_hoopCarrier_bubble_eq w' (hh.trans hh'.symm)
        (hcar.trans hc'.symm) (hb'.trans hj).symm).symm hj
    · right
      exact Prod.ext (w.reverseWand.eq_of_handle_hoopCarrier_bubble_eq w'
        (hh2.trans hh'.symm) (hcar2.trans hc'.symm) (hb'.trans hj).symm).symm hj
  · rintro (rfl | rfl)
    · exact he1
    · exact he2

omit [DecidableEq V] in
/-- Every wand event of the handle `Q` has an attached even hole as its hoop carrier. -/
theorem bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier_mem_attachedHoles {Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K}
    {e : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K × V} (he : e ∈ holeEvents G K Q) :
    bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2 ∈ attachedHoles G K Q := by
  obtain ⟨w, hb, hh, hev⟩ := (Finset.mem_filter.1 he).2
  rw [bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier_eq_hoopCarrier w hb hh, mem_attachedHoles]
  refine ⟨w.isEvenHoleCarrier_hoopCarrier hev, ?_⟩
  have := w.holeAttached_hoopCarrier
  rwa [hh] at this

/-- **The events of a handle are twice the attached holes, for an arbitrary summand.**
`∑_{events (P, j) with handle Q} g(C_{P,j}) = 2 ∑_{holes C attached to Q} g(C)`.  Unlike
`sum_holeEvents`, `g` need not be constant on deformation classes. -/
theorem sum_holeEvents_general {M : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M] (Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K)
    (g : Set V → M) :
    ∑ e ∈ holeEvents G K Q, g (bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2) =
      2 • ∑ C ∈ attachedHoles G K Q, g C := by
  rw [← Finset.sum_fiberwise_of_maps_to
    (g := fun e : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K × V => bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2)
    (fun e he => bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier_mem_attachedHoles he), Finset.smul_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun C hC => ?_)
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun e he => by rw [(Finset.mem_filter.1 he).2]), Finset.sum_const,
    holeEvents_fibre_card Q hC]

/-- Every attached hole is the hoop carrier of some wand event with handle `Q`. -/
theorem exists_holeEvent_of_mem_attachedHoles {Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K} {C : Set V}
    (hC : C ∈ attachedHoles G K Q) :
    ∃ e ∈ holeEvents G K Q, bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2 = C := by
  have h := holeEvents_fibre_card Q hC
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := Finset.card_pos.1 (by rw [h]; norm_num)
  exact ⟨e, (Finset.mem_filter.1 he).1, (Finset.mem_filter.1 he).2⟩

end Events

/-! ### Sector-balanced rows -/

namespace RootedInducedPath

/-- A coefficient row `c` on the rooted induced paths of `G*` is *sector balanced* when it is
balanced in the sense of `IsBalancedRow` (constant under single-vertex deformations, and under the
reversal of wands with an odd hoop) and moreover constant over the sources of one handle and one
deformation class of even hoops: if `w`, `w'` are bubble wands on `P`, `P'` with the same handle
and even hoops in the same deformation class then `c(P) = c(P')`.

For a graph with even holes these are the conditions under which the terms `h_P h_j` of the
clones and the odd hoops cancel in pairs and the even-hoop terms of one handle and class add up
to a generalized cycle operator `J_c` (v1 proof of Theorem 3, case (b.iv), L1555-1576).  The
rows `(A_λ^n)_{{j*},·}` of the corrected matrix are sector balanced
(`isSectorBalancedRow_cliqueHoppingMatrix_pow_root`). -/
def IsSectorBalancedRow {R : Type v} (c : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K → R) : Prop :=
  IsBalancedRow c ∧
  ∀ {P P' : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K} (w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P)
      (w' : CliqueBubbleWand G K P'), w.handle = w'.handle → Even w.hoopCard →
      Even w'.hoopCard →
      G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf w.hoopCarrier = G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf w'.hoopCarrier →
      c P = c P'

/-- A constant multiple of a sector-balanced row is sector balanced. -/
theorem IsSectorBalancedRow.const_mul {R : Type v} [Mul R]
    {c : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K → R} (hc : IsSectorBalancedRow c) (a : R) :
    IsSectorBalancedRow (fun P => a * c P) :=
  ⟨hc.1.const_mul a, fun w w' hh he he' hcl => by simp only [hc.2 w w' hh he he' hcl]⟩

end RootedInducedPath

/-! ### Rows are constant along the events of one handle and class -/

section Coefficients

open Classical

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v}

omit [DecidableEq V] in
/-- Two wand events with the same handle `Q` whose hoop carriers lie in one deformation class
have the same source coefficient, for a sector-balanced row. -/
theorem eq_of_mem_holeEvents {c : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K → R}
    (hc : RootedInducedPath.IsSectorBalancedRow c) {Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K}
    {e e' : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K × V} (he : e ∈ holeEvents G K Q)
    (he' : e' ∈ holeEvents G K Q)
    (hcl : G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf (bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2) =
      G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf (bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e'.1 Q e'.2)) :
    c e.1 = c e'.1 := by
  obtain ⟨w, hb, hh, hev⟩ := (Finset.mem_filter.1 he).2
  obtain ⟨w', hb', hh', hev'⟩ := (Finset.mem_filter.1 he').2
  refine hc.2 w w' (hh.trans hh'.symm) hev hev' ?_
  rwa [bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier_eq_hoopCarrier w hb hh,
    bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier_eq_hoopCarrier w' hb' hh'] at hcl

/-- The coefficient `c(P)` of a source `P` of the hole `C` at the handle `Q` (`0` if `C` is not
the hoop carrier of an event of `Q`).  By sector balance it does not depend on the source. -/
noncomputable def holeSourceCoeff [Zero R] (c : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K → R)
    (Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K) (C : Set V) : R :=
  if h : ∃ e ∈ holeEvents G K Q, bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2 = C then
    c (Classical.choose h).1 else 0

omit [DecidableEq V] in
theorem holeSourceCoeff_eq [Zero R] {c : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K → R}
    (hc : RootedInducedPath.IsSectorBalancedRow c) {Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K}
    {e : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K × V} (he : e ∈ holeEvents G K Q) :
    holeSourceCoeff c Q (bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2) = c e.1 := by
  have h : ∃ e' ∈ holeEvents G K Q,
      bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e'.1 Q e'.2 = bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2 :=
    ⟨e, he, rfl⟩
  unfold holeSourceCoeff
  rw [dif_pos h]
  obtain ⟨he', hφ⟩ := Classical.choose_spec h
  exact eq_of_mem_holeEvents hc he' he (by rw [hφ])

theorem holeSourceCoeff_eq_of_class [Zero R] {c : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K → R}
    (hc : RootedInducedPath.IsSectorBalancedRow c) {Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K}
    {C C' : Set V} (hC : C ∈ attachedHoles G K Q) (hC' : C' ∈ attachedHoles G K Q)
    (hcl : G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C = G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C') :
    holeSourceCoeff c Q C = holeSourceCoeff c Q C' := by
  obtain ⟨e, he, rfl⟩ := exists_holeEvent_of_mem_attachedHoles hC
  obtain ⟨e', he', rfl⟩ := exists_holeEvent_of_mem_attachedHoles hC'
  rw [holeSourceCoeff_eq hc he, holeSourceCoeff_eq hc he']
  exact eq_of_mem_holeEvents hc he he' hcl

end Coefficients

namespace PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation

/-! ### Commutators and a commuting right factor -/

section RightFactor

variable {A : Type w} [Ring A]

/-- `[H, X Pr] = [H, X] Pr` when `H` commutes with `Pr`. -/
theorem algebraCommutator_mul_right_of_commute {H Pr : A} (h : Commute H Pr) (X : A) :
    algebraCommutator H (X * Pr) = algebraCommutator H X * Pr := by
  unfold algebraCommutator
  rw [sub_mul, mul_assoc, mul_assoc, mul_assoc, ← h.eq]

/-- `ad_H^k (X Pr) = (ad_H^k X) Pr` when `H` commutes with `Pr`. -/
theorem iteratedCommutator_mul_right_of_commute {H Pr : A} (h : Commute H Pr) (X : A) (k : ℕ) :
    iteratedCommutator H k (X * Pr) = iteratedCommutator H k X * Pr := by
  induction k with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ n ih => rw [iteratedCommutator_succ, iteratedCommutator_succ, ih,
      algebraCommutator_mul_right_of_commute h]

end RightFactor

section Hoops

open Classical

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v} {A : Type w}
variable [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]

/-- `(-1)^n x = (-1)^n • x`, with the sign in `A` on the left and in `R` on the right. -/
theorem neg_one_pow_mul_eq_smul (n : ℕ) (x : A) :
    (-1 : A) ^ n * x = (-1 : R) ^ n • x := by
  rw [Algebra.smul_def, map_pow, map_neg, map_one]

omit [Fintype V] in
/-- **The even-hoop identity with the hole operator of the carrier**:
`h_P h_j = (-1)^{|C|/2 - 1} h_Q h_C`, where `h_C = holeOperatorOfCarrier C` for the hoop carrier
`C` of the wand (v1 L1555-1576; the sign is not displayed in v1).  This is
`pathOperator_mul_bubble_eq_holeOperator` with the labelling chosen inside the lemma. -/
theorem pathOperator_mul_bubble_eq_holeOperatorOfCarrier
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) {P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K}
    (w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P) (hev : Even w.hoopCard) :
    H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some w.bubble) =
      (-1 : A) ^ (w.hoopCarrier.ncard / 2 - 1) *
        (H.pathOperator w.handle * H.holeOperatorOfCarrier w.hoopCarrier) := by
  obtain ⟨k, E, -, hE, hop⟩ :=
    H.exists_fullCyclic_labeling_holeOperatorOfCarrier (w.isEvenHoleCarrier_hoopCarrier hev)
  have hk : w.hoopCard = 2 * k := w.hoopCard_eq_two_mul E hE
  have hn : w.hoopCarrier.ncard / 2 = k := by rw [w.hoopCarrier_ncard, hk]; omega
  rw [hn, hop, H.pathOperator_mul_bubble_eq_holeOperator w E hE]

/-- On an even-hole carrier the sector hypothesis reads `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr`. -/
theorem generalizedCycleOperator_mul_eq_of_isEvenHoleCarrier
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) (Pr : A)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    {C : Set V} (hC : G.IsEvenHoleCarrier C) :
    H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C) * Pr =
      lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C) • Pr := by
  obtain ⟨k, E, hE, rfl⟩ := (isEvenHoleCarrier_iff_exists_fullCyclic_labeling C).1 hC
  exact hJ k E hE

end Hoops

section SectorSums

open Classical

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v} {A : Type w}
variable [Field R] [CharZero R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]

/-- **The class sum of the hole terms.**  Let `γ` be constant on the deformation classes of the
holes attached to `Q`.  Then, on a sector (`J_c Pr = λ_c Pr`),
`∑_{C attached} γ_C (-1)^{|C|/2-1} h_Q h_C Pr = ∑_{C attached} γ_C (-1)^{|C|/2-1} (λ_c/|c|) h_Q Pr`.
The attached holes of a class are the whole deformation closure `⟨C₀⟩` (claim (i) of
`HoleAttachment.lean`), `∑_{C ∈ ⟨C₀⟩} h_C = J_c`, and `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr`
(v1 proof of Theorem 3, case (b.iv), L1555-1576). -/
theorem sum_attachedHoles_holeOperator_mul
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) (Pr : A)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    (Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K) (γ : Set V → R)
    (hγ : ∀ C ∈ attachedHoles G K Q, ∀ C' ∈ attachedHoles G K Q,
      G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C = G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C' → γ C = γ C') :
    ∑ C ∈ attachedHoles G K Q, (γ C * (-1 : R) ^ (C.ncard / 2 - 1)) •
        (H.pathOperator Q * (H.holeOperatorOfCarrier C * Pr)) =
      ∑ C ∈ attachedHoles G K Q, (hoopEventWeight G lam C * γ C) •
        (H.pathOperator Q * Pr) := by
  haveI : Fintype (EvenHoleDeformationClass G) := Fintype.ofFinite _
  rw [← Finset.sum_fiberwise (attachedHoles G K Q) (fun C => G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C)
      (fun C => (γ C * (-1 : R) ^ (C.ncard / 2 - 1)) •
        (H.pathOperator Q * (H.holeOperatorOfCarrier C * Pr))),
    ← Finset.sum_fiberwise (attachedHoles G K Q) (fun C => G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C)
      (fun C => (hoopEventWeight G lam C * γ C) • (H.pathOperator Q * Pr))]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun cl _ => ?_)
  by_cases hne : ((attachedHoles G K Q).filter
      (fun C => G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C = cl)).Nonempty
  · obtain ⟨C₀, hC₀⟩ := hne
    obtain ⟨hC₀a, hC₀c⟩ := Finset.mem_filter.1 hC₀
    obtain ⟨hC₀h, hC₀Q⟩ := mem_attachedHoles.1 hC₀a
    have hfil : (attachedHoles G K Q).filter (fun C => G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C = cl) =
        G.deformationClosureFinset C₀ := by
      rw [← hC₀c, ← attachedHoleFinset_eq_closure hK hclaw hC₀h hC₀Q]
      ext C
      simp only [Finset.mem_filter, mem_attachedHoles, Finset.mem_univ, true_and]
      tauto
    rw [hfil]
    have hmem : ∀ C ∈ G.deformationClosureFinset C₀,
        C ∈ attachedHoles G K Q ∧ InEvenHoleDeformationClosure G C₀ C := by
      intro C hC
      have hC' := hC
      rw [← hfil] at hC'
      exact ⟨(Finset.mem_filter.1 hC').1, mem_deformationClosureFinset.1 hC⟩
    have hcls : ∀ C ∈ G.deformationClosureFinset C₀,
        G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C = G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C₀ := fun C hC =>
      evenHoleDeformationClassOf_eq_iff.2 (hmem C hC).2.symm
    have hnc : ∀ C ∈ G.deformationClosureFinset C₀, C.ncard = C₀.ncard := fun C hC =>
      ((hmem C hC).2).ncard_eq.symm
    have hγC : ∀ C ∈ G.deformationClosureFinset C₀, γ C = γ C₀ := fun C hC =>
      hγ C (hmem C hC).1 C₀ hC₀a (hcls C hC)
    have hW : ∀ C ∈ G.deformationClosureFinset C₀,
        hoopEventWeight G lam C = hoopEventWeight G lam C₀ := by
      intro C hC
      unfold hoopEventWeight
      rw [hcls C hC, hnc C hC]
    have hJc := generalizedCycleOperator_mul_eq_of_isEvenHoleCarrier H Pr lam hJ hC₀h
    have hJsum : ∑ C ∈ G.deformationClosureFinset C₀, H.holeOperatorOfCarrier C =
        H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C₀) := rfl
    have hsize : (evenHoleClassSize (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C₀) : R) ≠ 0 :=
      Nat.cast_ne_zero.2 (evenHoleClassSize_pos _).ne'
    have hcard : (G.deformationClosureFinset C₀).card =
        evenHoleClassSize (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C₀) := (evenHoleClassSize_classOf C₀).symm
    have hL : ∑ C ∈ G.deformationClosureFinset C₀, (γ C * (-1 : R) ^ (C.ncard / 2 - 1)) •
        (H.pathOperator Q * (H.holeOperatorOfCarrier C * Pr)) =
        (γ C₀ * (-1 : R) ^ (C₀.ncard / 2 - 1) * lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C₀)) •
          (H.pathOperator Q * Pr) := by
      rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl (g := fun C => (γ C₀ * (-1 : R) ^ (C₀.ncard / 2 - 1)) •
          (H.pathOperator Q * (H.holeOperatorOfCarrier C * Pr)))
          (fun C hC => by rw [hγC C hC, hnc C hC]),
        ← Finset.smul_sum, ← Finset.mul_sum, ← Finset.sum_mul, hJsum, hJc, mul_smul_comm,
        smul_smul]
    have hR : ∑ C ∈ G.deformationClosureFinset C₀,
        (hoopEventWeight G lam C * γ C) • (H.pathOperator Q * Pr) =
        ((evenHoleClassSize (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C₀) : R) *
          (hoopEventWeight G lam C₀ * γ C₀)) • (H.pathOperator Q * Pr) := by
      rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl (g := fun _ => (hoopEventWeight G lam C₀ * γ C₀) •
          (H.pathOperator Q * Pr)) (fun C hC => by rw [hW C hC, hγC C hC]),
        Finset.sum_const, hcard, ← Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul R, smul_smul]
    rw [hL, hR]
    congr 1
    unfold hoopEventWeight
    field_simp
  · rw [Finset.not_nonempty_iff_eq_empty.1 hne]
    simp

end SectorSums


section EventSums

open Classical

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v} {A : Type w}
variable [Field R] [CharZero R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]

/-- **The even-hoop terms of one handle.**  For a sector-balanced row `c` on a sector
(`J_c Pr = λ_c Pr`),
`∑_{(P, j) wand events with handle Q} c_P h_P h_j Pr = (∑_P c_P (A_λ - T)_{PQ}) h_Q Pr`.
By `h_P h_j = (-1)^{k-1} h_Q h_C` (`PauliEvenHoopIdentity`), the events are twice the attached
holes (`sum_holeEvents_general`), and the class sum of `h_C` is `J_c` (v1 proof of Theorem 3,
case (b.iv), L1555-1576, with the sign and the normalisation of `CliqueHoppingMatrix.lean`). -/
theorem sum_holeEvents_pathOperator_mul
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) (Pr : A)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    {c : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K → R} (hc : RootedInducedPath.IsSectorBalancedRow c)
    (Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K) :
    ∑ e ∈ holeEvents G K Q, (c e.1 • (H.pathOperator e.1 * H.operator.term (some e.2))) * Pr =
      (∑ e ∈ holeEvents G K Q,
        hoopEventWeight G lam (bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2) * c e.1) •
        (H.pathOperator Q * Pr) := by
  set γ : Set V → R := holeSourceCoeff c Q with hγdef
  have h1 : ∀ e ∈ holeEvents G K Q,
      (c e.1 • (H.pathOperator e.1 * H.operator.term (some e.2))) * Pr =
        (γ (bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2) *
          (-1 : R) ^ ((bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2).ncard / 2 - 1)) •
          (H.pathOperator Q * (H.holeOperatorOfCarrier (bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2) *
            Pr)) := by
    intro e he
    obtain ⟨w, hb, hh, hev⟩ := (Finset.mem_filter.1 he).2
    have hcar := bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier_eq_hoopCarrier w hb hh
    have hE1 := H.pathOperator_mul_bubble_eq_holeOperatorOfCarrier w hev
    rw [hb, hh] at hE1
    rw [hcar, hγdef, ← hcar, holeSourceCoeff_eq hc he, hE1, hcar, neg_one_pow_mul_eq_smul (R := R),
      smul_mul_assoc, smul_mul_assoc, smul_smul, mul_assoc]
  have h2 : ∀ e ∈ holeEvents G K Q,
      (hoopEventWeight G lam (bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2) * c e.1) •
        (H.pathOperator Q * Pr) =
      (hoopEventWeight G lam (bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2) *
        γ (bubbleWandArcHoopCarrier e.1 Q e.2)) • (H.pathOperator Q * Pr) := by
    intro e he
    rw [hγdef, holeSourceCoeff_eq hc he]
  rw [Finset.sum_smul, Finset.sum_congr rfl h1, Finset.sum_congr rfl h2,
    sum_holeEvents_general Q (fun C => (γ C * (-1 : R) ^ (C.ncard / 2 - 1)) •
      (H.pathOperator Q * (H.holeOperatorOfCarrier C * Pr))),
    sum_holeEvents_general Q (fun C => (hoopEventWeight G lam C * γ C) •
      (H.pathOperator Q * Pr)),
    sum_attachedHoles_holeOperator_mul hK hclaw H Pr lam hJ Q γ
      (fun C hC C' hC' hcl => holeSourceCoeff_eq_of_class hc hC hC' hcl)]

end EventSums


section WandSplit

open Classical

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v} {A : Type w}
variable [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]

omit [DecidableEq V] in
/-- The terms of the *odd-hoop* wands cancel in pairs `(P, j) ↔ (P*, j_{s+1})` for a row with
`c(P*) = c(P)` for odd hoops (v1 L1575, "the contributions from odd holes cancel"); even hoops
are not summed here. -/
theorem sum_oddWand_smul_eq_zero
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A)
    (c : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K → R)
    (hrev : ∀ (P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K) (w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P),
      Odd w.hoopCard → c w.reverse = c P) :
    ∑ P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K, ∑ j ∈ P.wandBubbles,
      (if ∃ w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P, w.bubble = j ∧ Odd w.hoopCard then
        c P • (H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) else 0) = 0 := by
  rw [Finset.sum_sigma' Finset.univ
    (fun P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K => P.wandBubbles)
    (fun P j => if ∃ w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P, w.bubble = j ∧ Odd w.hoopCard then
        c P • (H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) else 0)]
  refine Finset.sum_involution
    (fun a ha => ⟨(a.1.wandOfBubble (Finset.mem_sigma.1 ha).2).reverse,
      (a.1.wandOfBubble (Finset.mem_sigma.1 ha).2).reverseBubble⟩) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_
  · rintro ⟨P, j⟩ ha
    have hj : j ∈ P.wandBubbles := (Finset.mem_sigma.1 ha).2
    set w := P.wandOfBubble hj with hw
    have hbub : w.bubble = j := P.wandOfBubble_bubble hj
    show (if ∃ w' : CliqueBubbleWand G K P, w'.bubble = j ∧ Odd w'.hoopCard then
        c P • (H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) else 0) +
      (if ∃ w' : CliqueBubbleWand G K w.reverse, w'.bubble = w.reverseBubble ∧
          Odd w'.hoopCard then
        c w.reverse • (H.pathOperator w.reverse *
          H.operator.term (some w.reverseBubble)) else 0) = 0
    by_cases hodd : Odd w.hoopCard
    · have key := H.pathOperator_mul_bubble_add_reverse_eq_zero w hodd
      rw [hbub] at key
      rw [if_pos ⟨w, hbub, hodd⟩, if_pos ⟨w.reverseWand, rfl,
        by rw [w.reverseWand_hoopCard]; exact hodd⟩, hrev P w hodd, ← smul_add, key, smul_zero]
    · rw [if_neg, if_neg, add_zero]
      · rintro ⟨w', hb', ho'⟩
        have : w'.hoopCard = w.reverseWand.hoopCard :=
          by rw [CliqueBubbleWand.ext_of_bubble_eq w' w.reverseWand hb']
        rw [this, w.reverseWand_hoopCard] at ho'
        exact hodd ho'
      · rintro ⟨w', hb', ho'⟩
        rw [CliqueBubbleWand.ext_of_bubble_eq w' w (hb'.trans hbub.symm)] at ho'
        exact hodd ho'
  · rintro ⟨P, j⟩ ha _ heq
    have hj : j ∈ P.wandBubbles := (Finset.mem_sigma.1 ha).2
    have := congrArg Sigma.fst heq
    exact (P.wandOfBubble hj).reverse_ne this
  · rintro ⟨P, j⟩ ha
    have hj : j ∈ P.wandBubbles := (Finset.mem_sigma.1 ha).2
    exact Finset.mem_sigma.2 ⟨Finset.mem_univ _, P.reverseBubble_mem_wandBubbles hj⟩
  · rintro ⟨P, j⟩ ha
    have hj : j ∈ P.wandBubbles := (Finset.mem_sigma.1 ha).2
    obtain ⟨e1, e2⟩ := P.wandOfBubble_involutive hj (P.reverseBubble_mem_wandBubbles hj)
    exact Sigma.ext e1 (heq_of_eq e2)

omit [DecidableEq V] in
/-- The sum over the bubbles of the wands with an *even* hoop, over all paths, is the sum over the
handles `Q` of the sums over the events `holeEvents G K Q`: every even-hoop wand event has exactly
one handle. -/
theorem sum_evenWand_eq_sum_holeEvents {M : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M]
    (F : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K × V → M) :
    ∑ P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K, ∑ j ∈ P.wandBubbles,
        (if ∃ w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P, w.bubble = j ∧ Even w.hoopCard then F (P, j) else 0) =
      ∑ Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K, ∑ e ∈ holeEvents G K Q, F e := by
  have h1 : ∀ P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K, ∑ j ∈ P.wandBubbles,
        (if ∃ w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P, w.bubble = j ∧ Even w.hoopCard then F (P, j) else 0) =
      ∑ j : V,
        (if ∃ w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P, w.bubble = j ∧ Even w.hoopCard then F (P, j) else 0) := by
    intro P
    refine Finset.sum_subset (Finset.subset_univ _) (fun j _ hj => ?_)
    rw [if_neg]
    rintro ⟨w, hb, -⟩
    exact hj ((P.mem_wandBubbles j).2 ⟨w, hb⟩)
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun P _ => h1 P), ← Fintype.sum_prod_type'
    (fun (P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K) (j : V) =>
      if ∃ w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P, w.bubble = j ∧ Even w.hoopCard then F (P, j) else 0)]
  have h2 : ∀ Q : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K, ∑ e ∈ holeEvents G K Q, F e =
      ∑ e : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K × V,
        if ∃ w : CliqueBubbleWand G K e.1, w.bubble = e.2 ∧ w.handle = Q ∧ Even w.hoopCard
        then F e else 0 := by
    intro Q
    unfold holeEvents
    rw [Finset.sum_filter]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun Q _ => h2 Q), Finset.sum_comm]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun e _ => ?_)
  by_cases hex : ∃ w : CliqueBubbleWand G K e.1, w.bubble = e.2 ∧ Even w.hoopCard
  · obtain ⟨w₀, hb₀, hev₀⟩ := hex
    rw [if_pos ⟨w₀, hb₀, hev₀⟩, Finset.sum_eq_single w₀.handle]
    · rw [if_pos ⟨w₀, hb₀, rfl, hev₀⟩]
    · intro Q _ hQ
      rw [if_neg]
      rintro ⟨w, hb, hh, -⟩
      exact hQ (by rw [← hh, CliqueBubbleWand.ext_of_bubble_eq w w₀ (hb.trans hb₀.symm)])
    · intro h
      exact absurd (Finset.mem_univ _) h
  · rw [if_neg hex]
    refine (Finset.sum_eq_zero (fun Q _ => ?_)).symm
    rw [if_neg]
    rintro ⟨w, hb, -, hev⟩
    exact hex ⟨w, hb, hev⟩

end WandSplit


section OneStep

open Classical

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v} {A : Type w}
variable [Field R] [CharZero R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]

omit [DecidableEq V] [CharZero R] in
/-- **One step of the commutator, before the hoop terms are resolved.**  For a row `c` that is
constant under single-vertex deformations, the clone terms of the exact one-row decomposition
cancel (`sum_deformation_smul_eq_zero`) and
`[H, ∑_P c_P h_P] = -2 ( ∑_Q (∑_P c_P T_{PQ}) h_Q + ∑_P c_P ∑_{j ∈ W(P)} h_P h_j )`
(v1 proof of Theorem 3, L1507-1518, in the convention `[H, ·]`). -/
theorem commutator_sum_eq_tree_add_wand
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A)
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (c : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K → R) (hc : RootedInducedPath.IsBalancedRow c) :
    algebraCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian (∑ P, c P • H.pathOperator P) =
      (-2 : R) • ((∑ Q, (∑ P, c P * cliqueTreeMatrix G K H.coupling P Q) • H.pathOperator Q) +
        ∑ P, c P • ∑ j ∈ P.wandBubbles, H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) := by
  have hlin : algebraCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian
      (∑ P, c P • H.pathOperator P) =
      ∑ P, c P • algebraCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian (H.pathOperator P) := by
    change commutatorLinearMap (R := R) H.physicalHamiltonian
      (∑ P, c P • H.pathOperator P) = _
    rw [map_sum]
    simp_rw [LinearMap.map_smul, commutatorLinearMap_apply]
  have hscalar : ∀ X : A, ((-1 : A) - 1) * X = (-2 : R) • X := by
    intro X
    rw [Algebra.smul_def, map_neg, map_ofNat]
    have h2 : ((-1 : A) - 1) = -2 := by rw [← neg_add', one_add_one_eq_two]
    rw [h2]
  have hdef := H.sum_deformation_smul_eq_zero c hc
  have htree : ∑ P, c P • ∑ Q, cliqueTreeMatrix G K H.coupling P Q • H.pathOperator Q =
      ∑ Q, (∑ P, c P * cliqueTreeMatrix G K H.coupling P Q) • H.pathOperator Q := by
    simp_rw [Finset.smul_sum, smul_smul, Finset.sum_smul]
    exact Finset.sum_comm
  rw [hlin]
  simp_rw [H.commutator_pathOperator_decomposition hK hclaw, hscalar]
  have hsplit : ∀ P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K,
      c P • (-2 : R) •
          ((∑ Q, cliqueTreeMatrix G K H.coupling P Q • H.pathOperator Q) +
            (∑ j ∈ P.deformationBubbles, H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) +
            ∑ j ∈ P.wandBubbles, H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) =
        (-2 : R) • ((c P • ∑ Q, cliqueTreeMatrix G K H.coupling P Q • H.pathOperator Q) +
          (c P • ∑ j ∈ P.deformationBubbles,
            H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) +
          c P • ∑ j ∈ P.wandBubbles, H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) := by
    intro P
    rw [smul_comm (c P) (-2 : R)]
    simp only [smul_add]
  simp_rw [hsplit]
  have hdef' : ∑ P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K,
      c P • ∑ j ∈ P.deformationBubbles, H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j) = 0 := by
    simpa only [Finset.smul_sum] using hdef
  rw [← Finset.smul_sum, Finset.sum_add_distrib, Finset.sum_add_distrib, hdef', add_zero, htree]

/-- **The wand terms on a sector.**  For a sector-balanced row `c`, on a sector
(`[H, Pr] = 0` is not needed here; `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr` is),
`(∑_P c_P ∑_{j ∈ W(P)} h_P h_j) Pr = ∑_Q (∑_P c_P (A_λ - T)_{PQ}) h_Q Pr`:
the odd hoops cancel in pairs (`sum_oddWand_smul_eq_zero`) and the even hoops of one handle add
up to `λ_c h_Q` (`sum_holeEvents_pathOperator_mul`).  (v1 proof of Theorem 3, case (b.iv),
L1527-1576.) -/
theorem sum_wand_mul_eq_hoop
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) (Pr : A)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    {c : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K → R} (hc : RootedInducedPath.IsSectorBalancedRow c) :
    (∑ P, c P • ∑ j ∈ P.wandBubbles, H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) * Pr =
      ∑ Q, (∑ P, (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam P Q -
        cliqueTreeMatrix G K H.coupling P Q) * c P) • (H.pathOperator Q * Pr) := by
  -- split every wand term into the odd and the even hoop part
  have hsplit : ∀ (P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K), ∀ j ∈ P.wandBubbles,
      c P • (H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) =
        (if ∃ w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P, w.bubble = j ∧ Odd w.hoopCard then
          c P • (H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) else 0) +
        (if ∃ w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P, w.bubble = j ∧ Even w.hoopCard then
          c P • (H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) else 0) := by
    intro P j hj
    obtain ⟨w, hb⟩ := (P.mem_wandBubbles j).1 hj
    rcases Nat.even_or_odd w.hoopCard with hev | hodd
    · rw [if_neg, if_pos ⟨w, hb, hev⟩, zero_add]
      rintro ⟨w', hb', ho'⟩
      rw [CliqueBubbleWand.ext_of_bubble_eq w' w (hb'.trans hb.symm)] at ho'
      exact (Nat.not_even_iff_odd.2 ho') hev |>.elim
    · rw [if_pos ⟨w, hb, hodd⟩, if_neg, add_zero]
      rintro ⟨w', hb', he'⟩
      rw [CliqueBubbleWand.ext_of_bubble_eq w' w (hb'.trans hb.symm)] at he'
      exact (Nat.not_even_iff_odd.2 hodd) he'
  have h1 : ∑ P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K, c P • ∑ j ∈ P.wandBubbles,
        H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j) =
      ∑ P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K, ∑ j ∈ P.wandBubbles,
        ((if ∃ w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P, w.bubble = j ∧ Odd w.hoopCard then
          c P • (H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) else 0) +
        (if ∃ w : CliqueBubbleWand G K P, w.bubble = j ∧ Even w.hoopCard then
          c P • (H.pathOperator P * H.operator.term (some j)) else 0)) := by
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun P _ => ?_)
    rw [Finset.smul_sum]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun j hj => hsplit P j hj)
  have hodd := sum_oddWand_smul_eq_zero H c hc.1.2
  simp_rw [Finset.sum_add_distrib] at h1
  rw [h1, hodd, zero_add, sum_evenWand_eq_sum_holeEvents
    (fun e => c e.1 • (H.pathOperator e.1 * H.operator.term (some e.2))), Finset.sum_mul]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun Q _ => ?_)
  have hsum := sum_hoopEntry_mul (RingHom.id R) H.coupling lam Q c
  simp only [RingHom.id_apply] at hsum
  rw [Finset.sum_mul, sum_holeEvents_pathOperator_mul hK hclaw H Pr lam hJ hc Q, ← hsum]


/-- **One step of the commutator on a sector** (the induction step of the proof of Theorem 3,
v1 L1494-1576, in the convention `[H, ·]`).  Let `c` be a sector-balanced row, `[H, Pr] = 0` and
`J_c Pr = λ_c Pr` for the classes of even holes.  Then
`[H, ∑_P c_P h_P Pr] = ∑_Q (-2 ∑_P c_P (A_λ)_{PQ}) h_Q Pr`
with `A_λ = cliqueHoppingMatrix G K b lam` the corrected matrix of Eq. (decoratedtree). -/
theorem commutator_sum_mul_of_isSectorBalancedRow
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) (Pr : A)
    (hHP : Commute H.physicalHamiltonian Pr) (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    {c : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K → R} (hc : RootedInducedPath.IsSectorBalancedRow c) :
    algebraCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian (∑ P, c P • (H.pathOperator P * Pr)) =
      ∑ Q, ((-2 : R) * ∑ P, c P * cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam P Q) •
        (H.pathOperator Q * Pr) := by
  have hsum : ∑ P, c P • (H.pathOperator P * Pr) = (∑ P, c P • H.pathOperator P) * Pr := by
    rw [Finset.sum_mul]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun P _ => (smul_mul_assoc _ _ _).symm)
  rw [hsum, algebraCommutator_mul_right_of_commute hHP,
    commutator_sum_eq_tree_add_wand H hK hclaw c hc.1, smul_mul_assoc, add_mul,
    sum_wand_mul_eq_hoop hK hclaw H Pr lam hJ hc, Finset.sum_mul, ← Finset.sum_add_distrib,
    Finset.smul_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun Q _ => ?_)
  have hscal : ∑ P, c P * cliqueTreeMatrix G K H.coupling P Q +
      ∑ P, (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam P Q -
        cliqueTreeMatrix G K H.coupling P Q) * c P =
      ∑ P, c P * cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam P Q := by
    rw [← Finset.sum_add_distrib]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun P _ => by ring)
  rw [smul_mul_assoc, ← add_smul, hscal, smul_smul]

end OneStep

end PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation

/-! ### The rows of the powers of `A_λ` are sector balanced -/

section Rows

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v} [Field R]
variable [DecidableEq (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K)]

/-- The rows `(A_λ^n)_{{j*}, ·}` of the corrected matrix are sector balanced
(`RootedInducedPath.IsSectorBalancedRow`): constant along deformation closures and under wand
reversals (v1 Lemma `deformationclosurepathsrelation` and Eq. (pathcircle), via the closed form
`krylovRow_mul_sectorIndepSeries`), and constant across the sources of one handle and one class of
even hoops. -/
theorem isSectorBalancedRow_cliqueHoppingMatrix_pow_root
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree) (b : V → R)
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R) (n : ℕ) :
    RootedInducedPath.IsSectorBalancedRow
      (fun P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K =>
        (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K b lam ^ n) (cliqueRootPath G K) P) := by
  refine ⟨⟨fun P s i h => ?_, fun P w _ => ?_⟩, fun w w' hh he he' hcl => ?_⟩
  · exact (sectorRow_pow_eq_of_closure hK hclaw b lam
      (InducedPathDeformationStep.inClosure ⟨s, i, h, rfl⟩) n).symm
  · exact (sectorRow_pow_wandReverse hK hclaw b lam w n).symm
  · exact sectorRow_pow_eq_of_sameHandle hK hclaw b lam w w' hh he he' hcl n

end Rows


namespace PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation

section Concrete

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v} {A : Type w}
variable [Field R] [CharZero R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
variable [DecidableEq (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K)]

/-- **Theorem 3 of v1 (Polynomial Divisibility) on a symmetry sector, concrete form** (v1
L1328-1336, proof L1494-1576; Result 2, L110-127), for a general finite claw-free graph `G`
with a simplicial clique `K` and a Pauli clique Hamiltonian representation `H`.

Let `Pr` be an element of the operator algebra with
* `[H, Pr] = 0`, and
* `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr` for the generalized cycle operator `J_c = ∑_{C ∈ c} h_C` of every class
  `c` of even holes (stated for the class of the carrier of every alternating labelling with full
  cyclic order, that is, of every even hole).

Then for every `k`, in the Lean convention `[H, ·]` (without the factor `i` of `[iH, ·]`),
`[H, ·]^k (χ) · Pr = (-2)^k ∑_P ((A_λ^k)_{{j*}, P}) h_P Pr`,
where `A_λ = cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam` is the corrected matrix of Eq.
(decoratedtree) (`CliqueHoppingMatrix.lean`: sign `(-1)^{k-1}`, root-handle arcs, per-event
normalisation `1/|c|`).  `A_λ` is real for real `λ` (`cliqueHoppingMatrix_map`) and bipartite by
the parity of the path length (`cliqueHoppingMatrix_ne_zero_imp_odd`); see
`paperTheorem3_of_commute_exists` for the existential form of v1.

*Proof.*  Induction on `k` with the good-row lemma
`iteratedCommutator_eq_matrixPow_sum_of_rows`, in the basis `P ↦ h_P Pr`.  Since `[H, Pr] = 0`,
`[H, X Pr] = [H, X] Pr`.  One step on a sector-balanced row
(`commutator_sum_mul_of_isSectorBalancedRow`): the tree part gives the tree matrix; the clone
terms cancel in pairs; the terms of the odd wands cancel in pairs (`P ↔ P*`); and the terms of the
even wands of one handle `Q` and class `c` add up to `2 (-1)^{k-1} h_Q J_c`, which on the sector
is `2 (-1)^{k-1} λ_c h_Q`, the column total of the hoop part of `A_λ`
(`sum_holeEvents_pathOperator_mul`).  The rows `(A_λ^n)_{{j*}, ·}` are sector balanced
(`isSectorBalancedRow_cliqueHoppingMatrix_pow_root`, from the closed form
`krylovRow_mul_sectorIndepSeries`).

*Fidelity.*  The unqualified name `paperTheorem3` is reserved for the statement of v1, in which
`Pr = Π_𝒥` is the joint spectral projector of the `J_c`; that statement needs `[H, Π_𝒥] = 0`,
which here is the explicit premise `hHP` (for `Π_𝒥` it follows from Theorem 1(ii),
`[H, J_c] = 0`, see `paperTheorem3_of_cycleAlgebra`).  `Pr² = Pr` is not needed and
not assumed, and the theorem holds for every such `Pr`.  The reading of "over each mutual
eigenspace" as right multiplication by `Pr` is forced by the statement: `J_c` need not commute
with the individual path operators `h_P`, so no left projection of `∑_P c_P h_P` is meaningful.
The matrix is the corrected matrix of `CliqueHoppingMatrix.lean`, not the printed one: the printed
Eq. (decoratedtree) misses the sign and the root arcs and is normalised per target, and with it
the identity fails already for the four-cycle with an edge clique. -/
theorem paperTheorem3_of_commute
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) (Pr : A)
    (hHP : Commute H.physicalHamiltonian Pr) (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    (k : ℕ) :
    iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator * Pr =
      ∑ P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K,
        ((-2 : R) ^ k * (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam ^ k) (cliqueRootPath G K) P) •
          (H.pathOperator P * Pr) := by
  set M : Matrix (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K) (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K) R :=
    cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam with hM
  set T : Matrix (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K) (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K) R :=
    (-2 : R) • M with hT
  have hpow : ∀ n : ℕ, T ^ n = (-2 : R) ^ n • M ^ n := fun n => by rw [hT, smul_pow]
  have hrow : ∀ n : ℕ,
      algebraCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian
          (∑ y, (T ^ n) (cliqueRootPath G K) y • (H.pathOperator y * Pr)) =
        ∑ y, (T ^ (n + 1)) (cliqueRootPath G K) y • (H.pathOperator y * Pr) := by
    intro n
    have hbal := (isSectorBalancedRow_cliqueHoppingMatrix_pow_root hK hclaw H.coupling lam
      n).const_mul ((-2 : R) ^ n)
    have key := H.commutator_sum_mul_of_isSectorBalancedRow hK hclaw Pr hHP lam hJ hbal
    simp only [hpow, Matrix.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]
    rw [key]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun Q _ => ?_)
    congr 1
    have hstep : (M ^ (n + 1)) (cliqueRootPath G K) Q =
        ∑ P, (M ^ n) (cliqueRootPath G K) P * M P Q := by
      rw [pow_succ, Matrix.mul_apply]
    rw [hstep, pow_succ, Finset.mul_sum, Finset.mul_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun P _ => ?_)
    ring
  have := iteratedCommutator_eq_matrixPow_sum_of_rows H.physicalHamiltonian
    (fun P => H.pathOperator P * Pr) T (cliqueRootPath G K) hrow k
  simp only [H.pathOperator_cliqueRootPath] at this
  rw [← iteratedCommutator_mul_right_of_commute hHP, this]
  simp only [hpow, Matrix.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul]

end Concrete


section CycleAlgebra

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v} {A : Type w}
variable [Field R] [CharZero R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
variable [DecidableEq (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K)]

omit [CharZero R] [DecidableEq (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K)] in
/-- **`[H, Pr] = 0` from Theorem 1(ii)**: every element of the subalgebra generated by the
generalized cycle operators `J_c` of the even holes commutes with the physical Hamiltonian,
because `[H, J_c] = 0` (`PauliFrustrationRepresentation.hamiltonian_commute_generalizedCycleSymmetryOp`,
v1 Theorem 1(ii)). -/
theorem commute_physicalHamiltonian_of_mem_adjoin
    (hclaw : G.IsClawFree) (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) {Pr : A}
    (hPr : Pr ∈ Algebra.adjoin R
      {J : A | ∃ C : Set V, G.IsEvenHoleCarrier C ∧
        J = H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C)}) :
    Commute H.physicalHamiltonian Pr := by
  have hle : Algebra.adjoin R
      {J : A | ∃ C : Set V, G.IsEvenHoleCarrier C ∧
        J = H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C)} ≤
      Subalgebra.centralizer R {H.physicalHamiltonian} := by
    refine Algebra.adjoin_le ?_
    rintro J ⟨C, hC, rfl⟩
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Subalgebra.mem_centralizer_iff]
    intro g hg
    rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff.1 hg]
    have h := H.operator.restrictSome.hamiltonian_commute_generalizedCycleSymmetryOp hclaw hC
    rw [generalizedCycleOperator_mk]
    unfold algebraCommutator at h
    exact sub_eq_zero.1 h
  have := hle hPr
  rw [Subalgebra.mem_centralizer_iff] at this
  exact this H.physicalHamiltonian rfl

/-- **Theorem 3 of v1 on a symmetry sector, for `Pr` in the algebra generated by the cycle
operators.**  The same conclusion as `paperTheorem3_of_commute`, with `[H, Pr] = 0` discharged by
Theorem 1(ii): `Pr` is any element of the subalgebra generated by the generalized cycle operators
`J_c` of the even holes (for example the joint spectral projector `Π_𝒥`, which is a polynomial
in the commuting `J_c`) on which `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr`.

The name stays qualified because `Pr` is assumed to lie in the algebra generated by the `J_c`; the
joint spectral projector of v1 is a polynomial in the `J_c` (Lagrange interpolation, see
`JointSpectralProjections.lean`), but the abstract operator algebra `A` has no spectral theory, so
this membership is a hypothesis about `Pr`. -/
theorem paperTheorem3_of_cycleAlgebra
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) (Pr : A)
    (hPr : Pr ∈ Algebra.adjoin R
      {J : A | ∃ C : Set V, G.IsEvenHoleCarrier C ∧
        J = H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf C)})
    (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → R)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr)
    (k : ℕ) :
    iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator * Pr =
      ∑ P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K,
        ((-2 : R) ^ k * (cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam ^ k) (cliqueRootPath G K) P) •
          (H.pathOperator P * Pr) :=
  paperTheorem3_of_commute hK hclaw H Pr
    (commute_physicalHamiltonian_of_mem_adjoin hclaw H hPr) lam hJ k

end CycleAlgebra

section Existential

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {A : Type w}
variable [Ring A] [Algebra ℂ A] [Algebra ℝ A] [IsScalarTower ℝ ℂ A]
variable [DecidableEq (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K)]

/-- **Theorem 3 of v1 on a symmetry sector, existential form** (v1 L1328-1336).  Over `ℝ`, for
`Pr` with `[H, Pr] = 0` and `J_c Pr = λ_c Pr` (`λ_c` real) there exists a real matrix `M`, indexed
by the rooted induced paths of `G* = G + j*`, which is the weighted adjacency matrix of a directed
bipartite graph (every nonzero entry `M_{PQ}` has `|P| + |Q|` odd, so `|P| mod 2` is the
bipartition), such that for all `k`
`ad_{iH}^k (χ) · Pr = (-2i)^k ∑_P (M^k)_{{j*}, P} h_P Pr`,  with `ad_{iH} = [iH, ·]`.

The witness is `M = A_λ = cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam` (`paperTheorem3_of_commute`
gives the concrete form with `[H, ·]`).  The name is qualified because of the premises `hHP` and
`hJ` on `Pr` (`docs/PAPER_FIDELITY.md`); v1 takes `Pr = Π_𝒥`, the projector onto a mutual
eigenspace of the `J_c`. -/
theorem paperTheorem3_of_commute_exists
    (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K ℝ A) (Pr : A)
    (hHP : Commute H.physicalHamiltonian Pr) (lam : EvenHoleDeformationClass G → ℝ)
    (hJ : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), E.HasFullCyclicOrder →
      H.generalizedCycleOperator (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) * Pr =
        lam (G.evenHoleDeformationClassOf E.carrier) • Pr) :
    ∃ M : Matrix (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K) (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K) ℝ,
      (∀ P Q, M P Q ≠ 0 → Odd (P.path.card + Q.path.card)) ∧
      ∀ k : ℕ, iteratedCommutator (Complex.I • H.physicalHamiltonian) k H.rootOperator * Pr =
        ∑ P, ((-2 * Complex.I) ^ k * ((M ^ k) (cliqueRootPath G K) P : ℂ)) •
          (H.pathOperator P * Pr) := by
  refine ⟨cliqueHoppingMatrix G K H.coupling lam,
    fun P Q h => cliqueHoppingMatrix_ne_zero_imp_odd h, fun k => ?_⟩
  rw [iteratedCommutator_smul_left, smul_mul_assoc,
    paperTheorem3_of_commute hK hclaw H Pr hHP lam hJ k, Finset.smul_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun P _ => ?_)
  have hreal : ∀ (r : ℝ) (x : A), r • x = (r : ℂ) • x := fun r x => by
    calc r • x = r • ((1 : ℂ) • x) := by rw [one_smul]
      _ = (r • (1 : ℂ)) • x := (smul_assoc r (1 : ℂ) x).symm
      _ = (r : ℂ) • x := by rw [Complex.real_smul, mul_one]
  rw [hreal, smul_smul, mul_pow]
  push_cast
  ring_nf

end Existential


section Consistency

variable [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {R : Type v} {A : Type w}
variable [Field R] [CharZero R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
variable [DecidableEq (CliqueRootedInducedPath G K)]

/-- Consistency check with the even-hole-free case: for a graph without even holes the hypothesis
`hJ` is vacuous (there is no even hole), and `Pr = 1` commutes with `H`, so
`paperTheorem3_of_commute` specialises to the statement of `Theorem3EvenHoleFree.lean`, with the
tree matrix in place of `A_λ` (`cliqueHoppingMatrix_of_evenHoleFree`). -/
example (hK : G.IsSimplicialClique K) (hclaw : G.IsClawFree)
    (hfree : ∀ C : G.IndexedInducedHole, ¬ Even C.card)
    (H : G.PauliCliqueHamiltonianRepresentation K R A) (k : ℕ) :
    iteratedCommutator H.physicalHamiltonian k H.rootOperator =
      ∑ P : CliqueRootedInducedPath G K,
        ((-2 : R) ^ k * (cliqueTreeMatrix G K H.coupling ^ k) (cliqueRootPath G K) P) •
          H.pathOperator P := by
  have hnone : ∀ (k : ℕ) (E : EvenHoleLabeling G k), ¬ E.HasFullCyclicOrder := by
    intro k E hE
    obtain ⟨C, hC, -⟩ := E.isEvenHoleCarrier_of_hasFullCyclicOrder hE
    exact hfree C hC
  have := paperTheorem3_of_commute hK hclaw H 1 (Commute.one_right _) (fun _ => 0)
    (fun k E hE => absurd hE (hnone k E)) k
  simpa [cliqueHoppingMatrix_of_evenHoleFree hfree] using this

end Consistency

